findings.body:
After `SelectLightTheme`, the assertion reads `darkThemeView` and expects `"1"`. In light mode the dark button should be `"0"`, so this assertion fails on every run. The variable is named `lightIsSelected` but reads the dark button, which suggests a copy/paste slip. The selector should be `lightThemeView`.

::diff{file="firefox-ios/firefox-ios-tests/Tests/XCUITests/DisplaySettingsTests.swift" lines="46-54"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The Dark and Automatic checks below are correct. Only the Light check is wrong.

::suggestion{file="firefox-ios/firefox-ios-tests/Tests/XCUITests/DisplaySettingsTests.swift" lines="53-54"}
let lightIsSelected = app.buttons[AccessibilityIdentifiers.Settings.Appearance.lightThemeView].value
XCTAssertEqual(lightIsSelected as? String, "1")

The description says a new test case was created for `testCheckSystemThemeChanges` and that only the old test would be deleted. The diff contains no new test method and deletes nothing with that name. It only changes the TestRail link and one selector in the existing method. The TestRail ID also moves from `2337487` to `3298823`. I can't check that ID from the repo, so reviewers need to confirm it points at the intended case.

::diff{file="firefox-ios/firefox-ios-tests/Tests/XCUITests/DisplaySettingsTests.swift" lines="46-47"}

Either the description is stale or a test is missing. Either way the record of what changed does not match the code.

`testClipboard` used to call `checkCopiedUrl()` after `copyUrl()`. That call is removed, and the PR does not mention it. `testClipboard` is still listed in the Smoketest and Accessibility plans, so the smoketest coverage shrinks. The helper's body is guarded by `#unavailable(iOS 16.0)`, so on iOS 16+ the removed call was already a no-op. On iOS 15 and earlier, it was the only check that the copied URL matches the pasteboard.

::diff{file="firefox-ios/firefox-ios-tests/Tests/XCUITests/ClipBoardTests.swift" lines="66-88"}

If the call is removed because it is flaky or unsupported, say so in the description and consider a comment at this spot. If not, restore the call.

`checkUrl`, `copyUrl` and `checkCopiedUrl` are now `public`, but `ClipBoardTests` is an internal class and nothing outside the module calls them. The rest of the XCUITest suite uses plain `func` for helpers. This change is unrelated to deleting tests and makes the diff noisier.

::diff{file="firefox-ios/firefox-ios-tests/Tests/XCUITests/ClipBoardTests.swift" lines="10-18"}

Revert the three `public` modifiers to match the rest of the test target.

After this PR, `checkCopiedUrl()` has no live caller. Its only remaining reference is inside the commented-out body of `testClipboardPasteAndGo` (line 102). Either remove the helper or keep a live caller. Leaving a helper with no caller and a commented reference to it is the kind of leftover that confuses later readers.

::diff{file="firefox-ios/firefox-ios-tests/Tests/XCUITests/ClipBoardTests.swift" lines="40-62"}

If the commented-out `testClipboardPasteAndGo` is meant to come back, leave the helper and say so in a comment. Otherwise delete it with the commented block.

The Done tap and `navigator.goto(NewTabScreen)` have been swapped. Before, the test navigated to the new-tab screen while still in the settings page and then tapped Done. Now it taps Done first and then navigates. The PR description does not mention this. The change may be needed to stop the navigator from failing on the settings screen, but nothing in the diff shows that. Without the reason, a reviewer can't tell whether it is a fix or an accidental edit.

::diff{file="firefox-ios/firefox-ios-tests/Tests/XCUITests/HomePageSettingsUITest.swift" lines="151-158"}

Add a one-line reason in the PR description or a comment, or revert the reorder if it is not needed.
